    <dl>
      <dt>Resort type</dt><dd>Deluxe Villa resort in the Disney Springs area. Disney Vacation Club inventory is mixed with cash bookings.</dd>
      <dt>Address</dt><dd>Confirm the street address and check-in building on your reservation. The Carriage House is the main building. <span class="verify">[verify current address]</span></dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>A large resort of several neighborhoods, inspired by upstate New York spa and horse-racing towns. Preferred locations are listed as closer to Disney Springs or to the Carriage House and dining. Treehouse Villas sit in their own wooded section.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Deluxe Studios sleep 4; one-bedroom villas sleep 5; two-bedroom villas and Treehouse Villas sleep 9; three-bedroom Grand Villas sleep 12. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Studio: 1 queen and 1 double-size pull-down. One-bedroom: 1 king, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 twin-size pull-down. Two-bedroom: 1 king, 2 queens, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 twin-size pull-down. Treehouse: 2 queens, 1 queen-size sleeper sofa, 1 bunk bed and 1 twin-size sleeper chair. Grand Villa: 1 king, 4 queens and 1 queen-size pull-down.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Sassagoula River Cruise boat to Disney Springs, plus a walking path. Buses to all four parks, the water parks and Disney Springs. This is not a Friendship boat to EPCOT or Hollywood Studios.</dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>The Artist's Palette, The Paddock Grill, The Turf Club Bar and Grill, On the Rocks Pool Bar and Backstretch Pool Bar, all listed on Disney's official Saratoga Springs dining page</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>High Rock Spring Pool (128-foot slide) and the Paddock Pool (146-foot slide), plus 3 leisure pools at the Treehouse Villas, Congress Park and The Grandstand</dd>
