  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Saratoga Springs is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a Deluxe Villa near Disney Springs,</strong> with a boat and a walking path instead of only a bus.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who specifically want a Treehouse Villa.</strong> Official 2026 listings put them at nine adults, in the woods, at about $1,226 to $2,332 a night at full price, tax included.</li>
      <li><strong>People who will use two feature pools.</strong> High Rock Spring and the Paddock Pool both have long slides and zero-depth entry.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a studio.</strong> Official listings cap Deluxe Studios at four adults (a queen and a double-size pull-down).</li>
      <li><strong>You book a standard (not Preferred) building at the far end of the resort</strong> and expect a short walk to the Carriage House or to Disney Springs. This property is large.</li>
      <li><strong>A short walk to a theme park is the main draw.</strong> All four parks are buses.</li>
    </ul>
    <span class="ryan">[Ryan: who you think this resort is really for, from your own stays. Two or three sentences.]</span>
  </section>

